doc:sch-1-sec-4ja-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "4JA(2) Some indictable offences punishable by fine only may be dealt" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) If the defendant is convicted, the court may impose a pecuniary penalty of:  (a) not more than 60 penalty units for an individual or 300 penalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more than 300 penalty units for an individual or 1,500 penalty units for a body corporate; or  (b) not more than 120 penalty units for an individual or 600 penalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more than 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a body corporate.  Schedule 1  Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914" ;
    cof:pageNumber "11"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "8 Crimes Legislation Enhancement Act 2003"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-8 ;
    values:originalText "However, the court may not impose a pecuniary penalty greater than the penalty that could have been imposed if the offence had been prosecuted on indictment.  (3) This section has effect subject to any contrary intention indicated by the law creating the offence.  (4) Without limiting subsection (3), this section does not apply to an indictable offence:  (a) created by a law that provides that the offence may be heard and determined by a court of summary jurisdiction; or  (b) described in subsection 4J(4) (about offences relating to property valued at $5,000 or less)." ;
    skos:definition "However, the court may not impose a pecuniary penalty greater than the penalty that could have been imposed if the offence had been prosecuted on indictment.  (3) This section has effect subject to any contrary intention indicated by the law creating the offence.  (4) Without limiting subsection (3), this section does not apply to an indictable offence:  (a) created by a law that provides that the offence may be heard and determined by a court of summary jurisdiction; or  (b) described in subsection 4J(4) (about offences relating to property valued at $5,000 or less)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "42c282aec8bb93052561ccaa8ac99d8c045b09067519a906a4449eed31c6109a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer ;
